police in California say another mass  shooting may have been averted officers  arrested 37 year old Rodolfo Montoya  he's a cook at a Marriott in Long Beach  at his home they found several guns and  ammunition now his arrest is one of the  latest in a string of mass shooting  threats after deadly attacks in El Paso  Texas and Dayton Ohio  CBS this morning national correspondent  Jericka Duncan is here tarika how  exactly did they find Montoya well Toya  Montoya basically told a co-worker  Monday he planned to come into work and  shoot everybody he saw at the hotel  because of a so called Human Resources  issue while that co-worker  notified Long Beach police who the next  day arrested Montoya at the RV where he  lives and confiscated an arsenal of  weapons suspect Montoya had clear plans  intent and the means to carry out an act  of violence that may have resulted in a  mass casualty incident Long Beach Police  arrested disgruntled hotel cook Rodolfo  Montoya at his home in Huntington Beach  they seized multiple high-powered  firearms hundreds of rounds of  ammunition and tactical gear including  an assault rifle and high-capacity  magazines which are illegal in  California  Irma Escobedo worked with Montoya at the  Marriott hotel she says he sometimes  made her uncomfortable but she never  reported him he looked for me and he  touched me or gave me a kiss on the head  I said don't touch me please don't don't  kiss me because the cameras out of there  and I don't like that one of the  suspects neighbors who did not want to  be shown says another neighbor warned  him to stay away from Montoya one next  door told me that he had guns in that RV  and stay clear that he's got all kinds  of guns now at least 29 people have been  arrested in 18 states for threatening  mass violence since mass shootings this  month in Texas and Ohio in Orlando  Wednesday a 16 year old girl was  arrested for allegedly threatening to  shoot people in her sister's Catholic  school according to the arrest report  she said in a group text next person to  say something is the first person I will  shoot on the school shooting that will  take place this Friday  as for Montoya we reached out to  Marriott but they have not  given us a comment police would not  confirm whether Montoya was about to be  fired and that's why he was upset but  when it was brought up at a press  conference on Wednesday the hotel's  general manager nodded his head Anthony  Jericka thank you
 

